    "title": "Thrombectomy / Embolectomy",
    "content": "Thrombectomy / Embolectomy\n\n### Sample Report 1\n\n**PREOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS:**\n[e.g., Acute right lower extremity ischemia due to thromboembolism]\n\n**POSTOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS:**\n[Same]\n\n**PROCEDURE PERFORMED:**\n[e.g., Right femoral artery thromboembolectomy with Fogarty balloon catheter]\n\n**SURGEON:** Oliver Aalami, MD\n**ASSISTANT:**\n**ANESTHESIA:** General anesthesia\n\n**ESTIMATED BLOOD LOSS:**\n**FLUIDS:**\n**SPECIMENS:** [e.g., Thromboembolus sent to pathology]\n**DRAINS:**\n**COMPLICATIONS:**\n\n**INDICATIONS:**\n[Brief clinical history — acuity of ischemia, Rutherford acute classification, suspected etiology (embolic vs thrombotic), affected limb exam]\n\n**DESCRIPTION OF PROCEDURE:**\n[Detailed operative narrative — include:\n- Groin incision and exposure of CFA/SFA/profunda\n- Systemic heparinization\n- Arteriotomy (transverse vs longitudinal)\n- Fogarty catheter passes (proximal and distal, balloon sizes, number of passes)\n- Quality of inflow and backbleeding\n- Additional maneuvers if needed (tPA infusion, on-table angiography)\n- Completion arteriography findings\n- Arteriotomy closure (primary vs patch)\n- Fasciotomy if performed (indication, compartments)\n- Pulse assessment\n- Hemostasis and closure]\n\n**FINDINGS:**\n[Thrombus burden, inflow/outflow status, completion angiography results, compartment assessment]\n\n**DISPOSITION:**\n[e.g., Patient transferred to ICU for monitoring, on heparin drip]\n\n---"
