    "title": "Pulmonary Embolism Thrombectomy",
    "content": "Pulmonary Embolism Thrombectomy\n\n### Sample Report 1\n\n**PREOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS:**\nSaddle Pulmonary Embolism\n\n**POSTOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS:**\nSame\n\n**PROCEDURE PERFORMED:**\n1) ultrasound guided access of the right common femoral vein\n2) femoral vein angiogram\n3) Pre-close Perclose placement\n3) selection of the pulmonary artery\n4) Mechanical Suction Thrombectomy of the pulmonary artery with FlowTriever system\n5) Pulmonary angiogram\n6) Closure of the L CFA with a closure device\n\n**SURGEON:** Oliver Aalami, MD\n**ASSISTANT:**\n**ANESTHESIA:** local with sedation\n\n**ESTIMATED BLOOD LOSS:** 30 mL\n**FLUIDS:** no foley\n**SPECIMENS:** thrombus. Discarded\n**DRAINS:** None\n**COMPLICATIONS:** None\n\n**FINDINGS:**\nExcellent flow in pulmonary arteries post thrombectomy.\n\n**DESCRIPTION OF PROCEDURE:**\nAfter the administration of sedation the patient's right groin was prepped and draped in the usual fashion. Ultrasound was used to evaluate the right common femoral artery which was noted to be fully compressible with no intrinsic echos.\n\nThe right common femoral artery was accessed using ultrasound guidance with a micropuncture needle after infiltration of the planned site of access with 1% lidocaine plain. A micropuncture wire was advanced and a micropuncture sheath was placed. A fem-check angiogram showed our puncture to be in the mid common femoral vein with a patent external and common iliac vein.\n\nNext we exchanged for a Storq wire and up sized to a 6Fr sheath. Next we used a Bernstein catheter to select for the superior vena cava and exchanged for a long Amplatz wire. We then placed the Intri 24 Sheath. Next we used an MIV catheter to select through the R atrium and ventricle into the pulmonary artery and performed our first pulmonary angiogram which showed a large saddle embolus. We then selected for the R inferior lobe with a Storq wire and a Bernstein catheter and and advanced our FlowTriever and performed the suction/mechanical thrombectomy procedure retrieving significant amount of thrombus. This was continued until we did not pull back any more thrombus. A follow up pulmonary angiogram showed much improved flow in the pulmonary arteries.\n\nWe removed our wires and sheaths and closed the femoral vein with the previously placed perclose device and also used the inari FlowStasis device.\n\nManual compression was held for 10 minutes.\n\n**DISPOSITION:**\nPatient transferred to recovery in stable condition\n\n---"
